.TH XMR\-KEYS 1 2026-10-25 "blocktools 0.1.0" "blocktools manual"
.SH NAME
xmr\-keys \- xmr\-keys [\-\-net main|stage|test] [\-\-scan\-out FILE [\-\-restore\-height N]] < seed
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
 xmr\-keys [\-\-net main|stage|test] [\-\-scan\-out FILE [\-\-restore\-height N]] < seed
 stdout: one JSON line of PUBLIC data (address, public spend/view keys).
 (address + private view key, no spend key) to FILE, created new with mode 0600. The view key
 is secret (it reveals incoming funds), so it never goes to stdout or stderr.
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
stdout: one JSON line of PUBLIC data (address, public spend/view keys).
\-\-scan\-out writes a monero\-wallet\-rpc `generate_from_keys` request for a VIEW\-ONLY wallet
(address + private view key, no spend key) to FILE, created new with mode 0600. The view key
is secret (it reveals incoming funds), so it never goes to stdout or stderr.
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
 \-\-scan\-out writes a monero\-wallet\-rpc `generate_from_keys` request for a VIEW\-ONLY wallet
.fi
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
stdout: one JSON line of PUBLIC data (address, public spend/view keys).
is secret (it reveals incoming funds), so it never goes to stdout or stderr.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Measured on Linux by the EXAMPLES below (scripts/gen\-man.py runs them):
.TP
1
no status field
.PP
Not every tool uses the same code for bad input: some exit 1, others exit 2 (docs/FINDINGS.md D1\-14). Always read the last JSON status line. Status and failure codes: docs/REFUSALS.md.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
$ echo not a seed | xmr\-keys
# exit 1, no status field
.fi
.SH SECURITY NOTES
DANGEROUS: use at your own risk. Code that handles keys and signs transactions should always be read and audited by you before you trust it with real funds. Used incorrectly, it can destroy your money.
Used incorrectly (wrong address, huge fee, lost keys, wrong chain) you lose funds; verify every transaction.
It opens hostile wallet files and extracts secrets: run it only sealed and offline (./blocktools run).
Unit tests are evidence, not a substitute for your own review. See docs/SECURITY.md.
